--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHICH LICENSE APPLIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

MIT License (see LICENSE-MIT) -- the software:

  - Source code: *.coffee, *.js, *.html, and package/build files
  - Everything under src/, test/, examples/ and sketches/

  Sketches are programs, so they follow the code: anyone may copy one into
  their own work on MIT terms.

CC BY-SA 4.0 (see LICENSE-CC-BY-SA) -- the documentation:

  - *.md, and everything under docs/

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOT IN THIS REPOSITORY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The game built on CoffeeBEANS -- its story, challenges, art and music -- lives
in a separate repository under its own terms. In particular, the art belongs
to the artists who made it and is licensed to Robert de Forest for the game;
nothing here grants any right to it.

Neither license grants rights to the name "CoffeeBEANS" for a product of your
own. Build it, fork it, ship it -- under another name.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These keep their own licenses; nothing above changes their terms. CREDITS.md
lists who made them.

  Electron -- MIT -- https://github.com/electron/electron
    (installed by npm; a packaged build ships Electron's LICENSE and
    LICENSES.chromium.html, which cover Chromium and its components)

  CoffeeScript 2.7.0 -- MIT -- https://coffeescript.org
    (vendored as src/renderer/vendor/coffeescript.js)

  CodeMirror 6 and its Lezer, style-mod, w3c-keyname, crelt and
  find-cluster-break dependencies -- MIT -- https://codemirror.net
    (bundled into src/renderer/vendor/editor.js)

  @replit/codemirror-vim -- MIT -- https://github.com/replit/codemirror-vim
    (bundled into src/renderer/vendor/editor.js)

  font8x8 by Daniel Hepper, from Marcel Sondaar's VGA fonts -- public domain
    -- https://github.com/dhepper/font8x8
    (transcribed into src/runtime/font.coffee)
